{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/848814-inheritance-hacks-or-getting-the-suicide-out","id":848814,"title":"Inheritance Hacks (or getting the Suicide out)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-03-17T08:22:14-07:00","id":848814,"title":"Inheritance Hacks (or getting the Suicide out)","content":"<span style=\"color:#FF0000\">If you don't want to get sidetracked you can leave the editorializing out. Please don't attribute thoughts or motives to others. Post edited by moderator.</span><br /> <br /> Long story short, since there's nothing in the <a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/beast-the-primordial-prestige-edition/description\" target=\"_blank\">Kickstarter description </a>that makes suicide seem like it's a necessary feature of the game I've come up with some hacks for suicide free (or at least suicide not baked in) alternatives to Inheritances. Without further ado:<br /> <br /> <b><i>Death of a Beast</i></b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">A Beast\u2019s Horror is a scion of the Mother of All Darkness. As such Beasts are not easily killed. And even when they die, some portion of their essence continues on. </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">A Beast cannot really die unless the Heart of its Lair is destroyed while its merged with its Horror. </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">When a Beast dies in the mortal world of the Chronicles of Darkness, its soul, the Horror, undergoes a transformation into one of the Unfettered--ephemeral nightmares that slumber within abandoned Chambers in the Hive and stalk mortals through the Primordial Dream. </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">If a Beast\u2019s Lair is destroyed while the Beast is not merged with its Horror (a rare occurrence), its Horror dies. When this happens, the Beast\u2019s Lair trait immediately becomes zero, he loses all of his Lair Traits, and immediately gains the Soulless (Persistent) condition. While under the effects of the Soulless Condition, the Beast neither gains nor loses Satiety. He cannot employ Atavisms or Nightmares and are for all intents and purposes is a human. This condition persists until the Soulless Beast passes away (from natural or unnatural causes), he gains a new soul, or he is Claimed by an Unfettered or some other ephemeral entity that looks for such empty vessels.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">If a Soulless Beast gains a new soul it slowly transforms into human, replacing it\u2019s Satiety with an equal amount of Integrity and losing all Atavisms and Nightmares in the process but gaining Unseen Sense (Beasts).<br /> <br /> <b>The Beast Unfettered</b></span></span></span><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Becoming Unfettered is not a matter of retreat. All Horrors can withstand the loss of their human bodies (i.e., ignore the Initiating the Retreat section). They are, after all, the children of things ancient beyond description. The Unfettered otherwise operate as described in B:tP except as follows.</span></span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><i><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Lair:</span></i></span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Unfettered retain the Lairs that their Horror\u2019s dwelled in while their Beast\u2019s were alive. These forlorn places drift to the bottom-most part of the Hive where they lay forgotten at the ends of unused Primordial Pathways. Each of the Lair\u2019s Chamber still has the Lair Traits that it had while the Beast was alive but, the Unfettered cannot exert any control over them or employ them in any conscious manner. This is not a matter of statistic recorded on a description of the Unfettered but rather describes the den in which the Unfettered slumbers away its meals.</span></span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><i><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Slumber:</span></i></span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> Like Horrors, Unfettered will slumber once they\u2019ve consumed enough Essence to fill their reserve. They always return to their Lair to sleep. As more ephemeral version of its former self, an Unfettered\u2019s Size remains the same as its Size when it was a Horror.</span></span></span><br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <i><b>Second Chances</b></i><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Unlike other Soulless mortals, Soulless Beasts maintain tenuous connections to both the Temenos and the Primordial Dream (possibly untrue, more information possibly coming with Mage: the Awakening?). These connections take the form of crumbled and ruined Oneiroses and overgrown, seemingly abandoned Chambers. Horrors instinctively avoid such places but Unfettered and other, darker entities, are attracted to them. </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The vast majority of those few Beasts that find themselves Soulless do not remain so for very long. The Soulless are magnets for ephemeral entities that desire access to the living world of the Chronicles of Darkness. Of particular significance is that Soulless Beasts gain the Resonant Condition as soon as an Unfettered enters their corresponding Chamber in the Primordial Dream. </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">At that point the Unfettered may use its Influences to Strengthen the Chamber eventually bringing about the Open Condition. From there the Unfettered will Possess the Soulless Beast. If the no one notices a pattern of repeated Possession occurs until the relationship progresses to Controlled. Once a Soulless Beast has been Controlled by an Unfettered, the Unfettered can Merge with it.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>The Beast Rampant</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The effects of an Unfettered Merging with a Soulless Beast work exactly as the Merger is described in B:tP except as noted below. For all intents and purposes the Merger works in a similar manner to the process of Claiming.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><i><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Merger Effects:</b> </span></i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The Rampant may select one of the following three options for each Rank possessed by the Unfettered doing the Merging.</span></span></span><ul><li><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><i><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Armor:</span></i></span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> As described in B:tP.</span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><i><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Body Warp:</b> </span></i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The Rampant may select a Dread Power. See CofD and W:tF. This rule replaces those found in B:tP.</span></span></span></span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><i><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Increased Attribute:</span></i></span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> As described in B:tP.</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><i><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Increased Awareness:</span></i></span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> All Rampant gain this Merger effect for free.</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></li> </ul><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Rampant also retain access to any Atavisms or Nightmares that they had in life but lose any Numina that the Unfettered Merging with them possessed. They have an effective Lair rating of 0. </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Rampant otherwise operate exactly as described in B:tP. Many Rampant eke out short, brutal lives that frequently end on the tip of a Hero\u2019s spear. Occasionally other Beasts find Rampants and grant them succor within the confines of their Lairs allowing both of them to realize several mutual benefits. There are also persistent but unsubstantiated rumors that some few Beasts have found a way to raise Rampant up from their semi-human bestial nature back to full Beasthood, splitting the Merged being back into Beast and Horror again.</span></span></span><br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Some Rampant Specific Merits</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Guardian (2) </b>-- <i><i>Requires:</i> </i>True Friend, Rampant only. <i><i>Effects:</i> </i>Your character has been befriended by a Beast who looks after him He gains a limited form of Primordial Pathways that allows him to enter and leave her guardian\u2019s Lair at will. His guardian also provides for his upkeep by providing prey thereby reducing the rate at which he loses Satiety to 1 every 3 days.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Pet (2)</b> </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">--</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><i><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><i>Effects:</i> </span></i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Your character has befriended one of the Rampant and looks after her. This merit operates exactly like True Friend except that the Rampant gains a limited form of the Primordial Pathways ability which allows her to enter and leave the Beast\u2019s Lair at will. </span></span></span><i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><i><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Drawbacks:</span></i></span></span></i><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> Because Rampants can no longer really function in human society your character has taken on the responsibility for limiting her friend\u2019s impact. Not only must you feed your own Horror, you must also provide prey for your friend.</span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b><i>Inheritance</i></b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Beasts and Heroes are both interlinked through the monomyths that produced them. Their conflicts with one another are foreordained by destiny itself. If it goes on long enough Beasts either die, destroyed along with their Lairs by the Heroes that hunt them or they subvert the myth and turn it on its ear.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Subversion is accomplished in one of two ways: either the Beast embraces the wisdom she has been dealing out for so long and becomes one of the Sagacious or she throws wisdom to the wind and succeeds in becoming everything Heroes fear her to be, an Incarnate.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The Beast Incarnate (The Lesser Subversion)</span></span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Becoming Incarnate works exactly as described in B:tP with the following exceptions.</div></div> </div> </div></span></span></span><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The Beast\u2019s life isn\u2019t really subsumed inasmuch it evolves into the post-human state of a living nightmare.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The Beast must become the Apex of his region and build a Myth for himself as normal (see B:tP). But, not only must the Beast completely dominate a Hero in opposition to the monomyth\u2019s cycle, he must slay the Hero. And not just any Hero will do. The Beast must dominate and slay a Hero (or a Band of Heroes) who has (or have) slain at least 8 Beasts. Only after all three tasks have been accomplished can the Beast claim the prize of evolving into an Incarnate.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The Beast Sagacious (The Greater Subversion)</span></span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Humans aren\u2019t the only beings capable of learning lessons from a Beast\u2019s nightmare feeding. Introspective Beasts slowly learn about their hungers, their legends, and their relationship with Heroes. Similar to the path to becoming an Incarnate, the path to joining the ranks of the Sagacious requires that a Beast accomplish three difficult tasks.</div></div> </div> </div></span></span></span><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><i><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Heal the Hero:</span></i></span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> The Beast must engage with a Hero who has slain 8 or more Beasts and through repeated lessons, impart wisdom that slowly heals the Hero\u2019s soul. This is often accomplished by showing the Hero the harm she is doing to others around her as they suffer for her righteousness and obsessions.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">In game terms, this is accomplished by forcing the Hero through a number of Breaking Points designed to increase his Integrity, thereby healing his soul. The Beast\u2019s player and the storyteller should agree to a list of reasonable breaking points that make this possible. Some examples include: Saw the Beast save a mortal, Saw the Beast save a mortal while under Anathema, Saw the Beast save a mortal that the Hero\u2019s own actions put in danger, Saved from certain death by the Beast (-2), etc.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><i><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Subvert the Hero:</b> </span></i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The Beast must befriend a Hero whose Integrity is 7 or greater. Like Spawn Legend, the goalposts for this achievement are more subjective than objective. The player and the storyteller should agree on a number of quests (around three to five sounds about right) where the Beast overtly aids the Hero in conquering threats to humanity. These may be other Beasts but Rampants, and especially Unfettered, could also easily be acceptable menaces. The Beast must purchase the True Friend merit with any experiences earned through this process.</span></span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><i><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Conquer the Terror:</span></i></span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Finally, the Beast and the Hero he has befriended must overcome a dire threat to the Primordial Dream. These usually take the form of Incarnates but a particularly brutal Apex (whose Lair is 8 or more) or an Unfettered whose Rank exceeds 7 (i.e., Rank 8+) would also suffice. The duo don't need to kill the terror, it is sufficient to contain it indefinitely, but, they do need to work together in order to accomplish this goal.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><i><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Success: The Wisdom</b></span></i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Once these tasks have been accomplished both Beast and Hero emerge as something new that shakes off the clothing of myths and stories altogether. The become a paired being--The Beast Sagacious and The Paragon. Rather than a framework of reinforcing myths, their dual existence is maintained by a syllabary of lessons to be taught to both the human minds drifting in and out of the Primordial Dream and those things that stalk them.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The Sagacious gain a number of abilities that are the same or similar to those gain by Incarnates. These abilities include:</span></span></span><ul><li><b>Adopt the Beast-Shape:</b> Exactly as described for Incarnates in B:tP.</li> <li><b>Ethereal Voyager:</b> As long as she is in the presence of her Paragon, the pair may enter the Astral and voyage to any realm within it. (This includes the Primordial Dream and the Supernal Realms.)</li> <li><b>Intertwined Lives:</b> If either the Sagacious or the Paragon should die, the other dies too.</li> <li><b>Legend/Life:</b> Both the Beast and the Hero lose their Legend and Life and gain a shared combined trait called Wisdom. Both can regain Willpower through this trait exactly in the same way as they did through their Life traits.</li> <li><b>Master of Magic:</b> The Sagacious gains five dots in a single Arcana of his choice. The Sagacious also selects a number Spells equal in number to the number of Nightmares he knows (see M:tA; use Dread Powers and Numena instead if the troupe doesn\u2019t want to crossover with Mage: the Awakening).</li> <li><b>No More Heroes:</b> The Beast Sagacious has a completely different interaction with Heroes than the Beast Incarnate. Having achieved a form that no longer needs to feed on the suffering of others, Sagacious do not cause Heroes to awaken and Heroes are not drawn to them. As such Heroes cannot use their powers on Sagacious (or Paragons); however, as the duo very much appears to be a complete perversion of the natural order of things from a Hero\u2019s perspective, Heroes have been known to hunt them.</li> <li><b>No More Lair:</b> The Beast\u2019s Horror merges with her, precipitating a complete collapse of her Lair. She loses all invulnerabilities and Lair Traits associated with it. She uses her Paragon\u2019s supernatural tolerance trait--Anointment--in place of her Lair trait.</li> <li><b>Satiety:</b> Unlike Incarnates, Sagacious no longer need to feed at all. They replace their Satiety trait with an energy pool called Prudence. The size of this pool is 80 and both the Sagacious and her Paragon may draw upon it each turn. They may spend Prudence anytime they would spend Willpower or Satiety (or Mana) to employ an ability that calls for it. No more than 8 Prudence can be spent in any given turn. Anytime either the Sagacious or the Paragon could gain Willpower they may choose to gain Prudence instead. They also lose all of their Nightmares.</li> <li><b>Soul Sickness:</b> The Beast Sagacious does not suffer Breaking Points; however, its Paragon can and does suffer Breaking Points for any decisions that either of them make that would normally cause an Integrity Breaking Point. Because the Paragon has an Integrity trait, it is possible for the duo to fall from grace. For the Sagacious\u2019 part, this is experienced as a physical sickening. The Sagacious suffers one Aggravated wound each time its Paragon loses a point of Integrity. Should the Paragon\u2019s Integrity fall to zero, the Sagacious dies. In this case, the Paragon (or whatever they have become) lives on.</li> </ul><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">The Paragon (The Hero Ennobled)</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Heroes that learn the lessons taught by Beasts on the Sagacious path find themselves uplifted into something more than human but less than divine. This transfiguration forges the Hero into an extension of the Beast\u2019s will to teach lessons. This expresses itself through several abilities that the Paragon gains.</span></span></span><ul><li><b>Anathema:</b> Anathema provide a powerful incentivising tool for the Sagacious to use in place of Nightmares when teaching lessons. As such a Paragon may place an Anathema on any entity, mortal or supernatural. However, because their existence is so focused on teaching moments, the Paragon suffers a Breaking Point anytime he places an Anathema for a reason other than teaching a lesson.</li> <li><b>Anointment:</b> The Paragon gains a supernatural tolerance trait called Anointment. It\u2019s value is equal to the average of number of Beasts the Paragon had slain as a Hero and the Lair rating of the Beast who uplifted her.</li> <li><b>Heroic Tracking &amp; Stalking:</b> Since the purpose of their new lives is to teach lessons, the Paragon\u2019s ability to track and stalk subtly changes so that he can track and stalk any entity whose Integrity (or Integrity analogue, e.g., Humanity, Cover, Harmony, Satiety, etc.) is 3 or less. The Sagacious and their Paragons ignore entities with higher Integrities (or Integrity analogues), even if they\u2019re causing more harm. Ennoblement dulls the Paragon\u2019s senses to the \u201cwrongs\u201d of the world.</li> <li><b>Integrity:</b> As a metaphysically conjoined being, the Paragon must carry the burden of both of their actions. In addition to suffering through Integrity Breaking Points anytime his own actions would call for it, the Paragon must endure an Integrity Breaking Point anytime his Sagacious partner\u2019s actions would call for it.</li> <li><b>Intertwined Lives:</b> If either the Sagacious or the Paragon should die, the other dies too.</li> <li><b>Legend/Life:</b> Both the Beast and the Hero lose their Legend and Life and gain a shared combined trait called Wisdom. Both can regain Willpower through this trait exactly in the same way as they did through their Life traits.</li> <li>Prudence: The Paragon\u2019s Sagacious partner maintains a pool of spiritual energy called Prudence. The Paragon may draw upon this pool anytime they would be called upon to spend Willpower. Similarly, the Paragon may choose to replenish one Prudence to the pool anytime he could gain one Willpower for himself.</li> <li><b>Soul Shock:</b> Should the Paragon\u2019s Integrity ever fall to zero, her Sagacious partner dies. The resulting shock transforms the Paragon again, this time into a maniacal Slasher (see H:tV; the Paragon can gain the Soulless (Persistent) condition instead if the troupe doesn\u2019t want to crossover with Hunter: the Vigil).</li> </ul><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Once they have joined together and emerged as new dualistic being the Beast Sagacious and his Paragon spend their time giving lessons to those whose souls are near to destruction. These lessons aren\u2019t limited to mortals and the tools that the pair can employ are much broader than the subtle but often clumsy application of fear alone. They can inflict pain, praise, and employ any number of other techniques in pursuit of their task. Should the pupil prove intransigent enough, they can even employ the final lesson.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Like Incarnates, a Sagacious\u2019 existence is hardly secure. She is completely dependent upon her Paragon to bear the weight of both of their souls and can quickly die if it turns out that the Hero she chose ultimately wasn\u2019t equal to the task.</span></span></span><br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Feedback on these hacks is always welcome.<br /> <br /> I don't want to see this thread devolve into a debate about suicide though. It's a very personal and sensitive topic to those of us who have been touched by it. If folks want to discuss it specifically, please start a separate thread for it (preferably in the OPP OT area of the forums).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","user":"Darksider","date":". 03-17-2016, 02:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T10:20:44-07:00","id":848857,"title":"","content":"Seems kinda odd for the Beast Sagacious to pick up Mage traits of all things.<br /> <br /> Other than that, I kinda like it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T10:45:04-07:00","id":848870,"title":"","content":"I agree, it's very interesting. Just looking at the Unfettered, I can see a storyline arising out of one of them wanting to become a real Horror again so that it can become a part of a Beast. Thet's just my first thought though. The Beast Sagacious would be fantastic for a Gandalf-analogue mentor/bodhisattva character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T11:06:12-07:00","id":848883,"title":"","content":"I was going for the Gandalf, Shadowfax vibe.<br /> <br /> Regarding Mage magic. I knew I wanted them to have magic (enlightenment) and Mage was simply the system most intertwined with the Astral (of which the Primordial Dream is a part of). One could substitute something else (like cruac).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-19T00:11:06-07:00","id":849628,"title":"","content":"This is another interesting set of ideas from you. I might actually integrate this with some small tweaks of my own.<br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Keep up the good work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"